WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.502
A pre-existing condition is one for which the insured received medical advice,

00:00:05.502 --> 00:00:11.004
diagnosis or treatment, or had symptoms a prudent person would have treated,

00:00:11.004 --> 00:00:16.505
during a look-back period before coverage began, often six to twelve months.

00:00:16.505 --> 00:00:21.090
Older medical policies excluded such conditions for a waiting period.

00:00:21.090 --> 00:00:25.675
Federal law now forbids pre-existing condition exclusions in comprehensive medical

00:00:25.675 --> 00:00:29.802
coverage, so Marcus’s asthma is covered from day one.

00:00:29.802 --> 00:00:33.928
The exclusion still appears in disability income, long-term care,

00:00:33.928 --> 00:00:38.054
Medicare supplement, short-term policies and certain other limited policies.

00:00:38.054 --> 00:00:40.805
Each type has its own rules.

00:00:40.805 --> 00:00:45.390
Always check the type of coverage before applying the rule.

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:49.195
Policies exclude intentionally self-inflicted injuries, including injuries from a

00:00:49.195 --> 00:00:53.000
suicide attempt, because insurance covers accidental and unexpected loss.

00:00:53.000 --> 00:00:56.383
Mental health treatment for the underlying condition is

00:00:56.383 --> 00:00:59.342
a separate, covered matter under parity rules.

00:00:59.342 --> 00:01:03.570
Policies also exclude losses caused by war or an act

00:01:03.570 --> 00:01:07.798
of war, declared or undeclared, and often losses while serving

00:01:07.798 --> 00:01:11.603
in the armed forces, for which military coverage exists.

00:01:11.603 --> 00:01:16.254
If Rosa deliberately injures herself, her disability policy does not pay;

00:01:16.254 --> 00:01:20.905
if she is injured in a terrorist attack at home, most

00:01:20.905 --> 00:01:24.710
policies pay because that is not war between nations.

00:01:24.710 --> 00:01:29.962
Elective cosmetic surgery, chosen to change appearance without a medical need, is excluded.

00:01:29.962 --> 00:01:31.578
Reconstructive surgery is different.

00:01:31.578 --> 00:01:36.022
Repairing a face after an accident, correcting a congenital defect in

00:01:36.022 --> 00:01:40.466
a child, or rebuilding a breast after a mastectomy restores function

00:01:40.466 --> 00:01:44.910
or appearance lost to injury or disease, and these are covered.

00:01:44.910 --> 00:01:48.950
Maryland specifically requires coverage of reconstructive breast surgery after a

00:01:48.950 --> 00:01:52.586
mastectomy, including surgery on the other breast for symmetry.

00:01:52.586 --> 00:01:57.030
The question to ask is why the procedure is being done.

00:01:57.030 --> 00:02:01.070
A medical cause moves the claim out of the exclusion.

00:02:01.070 --> 00:02:04.092
Most individual and group health policies are nonoccupational.

00:02:04.092 --> 00:02:07.870
They exclude conditions covered by workers compensation, because that system

00:02:07.870 --> 00:02:11.270
is the primary payer for job-related injuries and illnesses.

00:02:11.270 --> 00:02:15.803
When Rosa is hurt on a job site, workers compensation pays her

00:02:15.803 --> 00:02:20.336
medical bills and partial wage replacement, and her health plan steps aside.

00:02:20.336 --> 00:02:24.491
Policies also exclude care furnished by government plans, such as treatment

00:02:24.491 --> 00:02:28.647
at a Veterans Affairs facility or under military coverage, and care

00:02:28.647 --> 00:02:32.425
for which the insured has no legal obligation to pay.

00:02:32.425 --> 00:02:36.580
The purpose is to avoid paying twice for the same loss.

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:40.045
Injuries sustained while committing or attempting a felony, or

00:02:40.045 --> 00:02:43.124
while engaged in an illegal occupation, are excluded.

00:02:43.124 --> 00:02:47.358
The uniform optional provision on illegal occupation, which Lesson 17 covers,

00:02:47.358 --> 00:02:51.208
lets the insurer deny a loss arising from such activity.

00:02:51.208 --> 00:02:54.287
A person injured while burglarizing a warehouse cannot

00:02:54.287 --> 00:02:57.367
collect medical or disability benefits for those injuries.

00:02:57.367 --> 00:03:00.832
The exclusion requires participation in the crime; a bystander

00:03:00.832 --> 00:03:04.296
or victim injured during someone else’s felony is covered.

00:03:04.296 --> 00:03:08.145
Some policies similarly exclude losses while intoxicated or under the

00:03:08.145 --> 00:03:11.610
influence of unprescribed narcotics, again through an optional provision.

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:15.927
Exclusions are lists of causes, not lists of body parts.

00:03:15.927 --> 00:03:19.381
To decide a claim, identify the cause of

00:03:19.381 --> 00:03:22.834
the loss, then check it against the list.

00:03:22.834 --> 00:03:28.015
Asthma under a comprehensive medical plan: covered, because pre-existing exclusions are gone.

00:03:28.015 --> 00:03:30.605
A deliberate overdose: excluded as self-inflicted.

00:03:30.605 --> 00:03:34.922
A scar revision after a dog bite: covered as reconstructive.

00:03:34.922 --> 00:03:39.239
A fall at work: workers compensation, not the health plan.

00:03:39.239 --> 00:03:43.556
A broken leg during a robbery the insured committed: excluded.

00:03:43.556 --> 00:03:49.168
When two exclusions seem to apply, the one that actually caused the loss

00:03:49.168 --> 00:03:54.780
controls, and the burden of proving an exclusion generally falls on the insurer.
